{
  "title": "Filtered mvn test runs can poison the Maven build cache as full \
results",
  "description": "The Maven build-cache extension caches surefire:test results \
keyed by source hash. A -Dtest=... filtered run saves a cache entry that a \
later unfiltered `mvn test` on the same sources replays ('Skipping plugin \
execution (cached): surefire:test'), silently skipping every test outside the \
original filter. Observed while adding GameSessionWatcherThreadingTest: a \
TEST=-filtered `make test-java` run was cached, and the follow-up full-suite \
run replayed it without executing the other Mage.Server tests. test-java now \
passes -Dmaven.build.cache.enabled=false for TEST-filtered runs, but `make \
verify-decks` still runs `mvn test -pl Mage.Verify \
-Dtest=\"VerifyCardDataTest#test_checkSampleDecks\"` without disabling the \
cache, so it can cache a filtered result as Mage.Verify's test outcome for \
that source hash. Audit remaining filtered mvn test invocations (Makefile and \
CI) and disable the build cache for any run that doesn't execute the full \
module suite.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "build",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-07-02T06:05:00.000000-07:00",
